    "code": "def sum_nested(items):\n    total = 0\n    for item in items:\n        if isinstance(item, list):\n            total += sum_nested(item)\n        else:\n            total += item\n    return total",
    "explanation": "Treat a number as a base case and a list as a request to sum its children recursively. This handles arbitrary nesting depth without flattening first. Empty lists contribute zero."
  },
